# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the Druid nano-quickstart with druid.javascript.enabled
# =true in _common (server-side JS execution on the query-serving nodes,
# CVE-2021-25646) and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the broker is ALREADY RUNNING with JS enabled when the agent starts. verify.sh
#     sends a real JavaScript-aggregator query to the LIVE broker (port 8082): while
#     JS is live-enabled the query executes, once JS is live-disabled the broker
#     returns "JavaScript is disabled". Because the flag is read only at process
#     start, a fix that edits runtime.properties but never restarts the broker leaves
#     JS live-enabled and the check FAILS — the not-restarted case is genuinely
#     detectable and graded.
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting Druid cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must set druid.javascript.enabled=false on the
# query nodes (_common) AND RESTART the Druid services, not merely edit the file.
